# Fetched data and the generated site are both rebuilt fresh by
# update_all.py every run (locally or in CI) -- committing them would just
# bloat the repo's history with constantly regenerated JSON/HTML for no
# benefit. Nothing here is a source file.
belt_data/
site/

# historical_data/ is DELIBERATELY NOT ignored -- it's the small, git-
# committed baseline (settled reigns/belt games + settled box scores +
# settled play-by-play) that lets build_lineage.py, fetch_game_details.py,
# and fetch_game_plays.py fetch only the current + previous season each run
# instead of CFBD's whole history every time. See README.md's "Incremental
# fetching" section.
#
# ai_preview_cache/ is also DELIBERATELY NOT ignored, same idea -- it's the
# last AI-generated upcoming-game preview, keyed to exactly which game it's
# for, so generate_ai_preview.py only spends a real Claude API call when
# the upcoming game actually changes instead of on every run.
#
# recap_cache/ is also DELIBERATELY NOT ignored -- one AI-written recap per
# settled belt game since 2003, keyed by game id, so generate_recaps.py
# never re-spends a Claude API call on a game it's already recapped.
#
# historical_data/us_state_shapes.json is a different kind of file in the
# same folder: it's not a fetch cache at all, it's permanent static
# reference data (US state boundary outlines, extracted once from the
# public-domain-derived bokeh_sampledata package -- see README.md's "Map"
# section) that build_site.py reads every run to draw the belt-history map.
# It never grows or gets refetched, so there's nothing to regenerate here.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

Claude outputs/
